{"timestamp":"2026-06-04T00:26:44.314Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"mdocs","args":{"command":"initiative.create","args":{"title":"PR Triage — Open PR Analysis and Merge Plan","id":"pr-triage-2026-06-03","owner":"system","tags":{"item":["pr-triage","dev-branch","agent-sprawl","code-quality"]},"objective":"Audit the 9 open PRs targeting `dev`, identify duplicates, assess value, detect potential merge conflicts, and produce a final merge-vs-close decision plan with an ordered merge sequence.","plan":"1. Inventory all open PRs (done at intake — 9 PRs identified).\n2. Cluster PRs by topic and detect duplicates by branch name, file overlap, and commit subject.\n3. Dispatch a subagent for a deep code-level diff review between duplicate clusters to confirm the canonical (most complete) version of each topic.\n4. Assess the value of each unique topic (security impact, performance, UX, a11y).\n5. Detect potential merge conflicts between non-duplicate PRs (e.g., do #138 and #135 both touch `svelte.config.js` and `hooks.server.ts`?).\n6. Produce a final decision table with merge order to minimize conflicts.\n7. Capture the agent-spawn duplication pattern as a wiki entry for the operational playbook.\n8. Update the initiative progress log and offer to mark done."}}}}
