{"timestamp":"2026-06-04T00:50:34.492Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/aerialdb && gh pr view 139 --json state,mergeable,mergeStateStatus,additions,deletions,changedFiles 2>&1 | head -10 && echo \"---\" && gh pr merge 139 --squash --delete-branch --subject \"⚡ Bolt: optimize database queries with db.batch() (#139)\" --body \"Squash-merged from #139.\n\nImplements Drizzle \\`db.batch()\\` in three load functions to consolidate multiple D1 round-trips into a single HTTP request:\n- src/routes/+page.server.ts: home page (3 round-trips → 1)\n- src/routes/admin/+page.server.ts: admin dashboard (2 round-trips → 1)\n- src/routes/admin/categories/+page.server.ts: category management (PR #139 is the only one of the four db.batch() candidates to cover this file)\n\nAlso augments the Database type in src/lib/server/db/index.ts to support the batch method in TypeScript with the correct \\`Promise<{ [K in keyof T]: Awaited<T[K]> }\\>\\` return type.\n\nPre-merge cleanup applied directly to this branch:\n- Removed unused \\`LeanMoveRaw\\` and \\`AdminLeanMoveRaw\\` type imports (the old \\`as [LeanMoveRaw[], ...]\\` cast was made unnecessary by the batch() return type).\n- Updated stale test comment in +page.server.security.spec.ts.\n\nCloses: supersedes #132, #133, #134 (parallel duplicate db.batch() PRs from the same dev head). #132 also had a path-case regression (.jules/bolt.md vs .Jules/bolt.md).\" 2>&1 | tail -20","description":"Squash-merge PR #139"}}}
