{"timestamp":"2026-06-04T00:51:30.760Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/aerialdb && gh pr close 132 --comment \"Closing in favor of #139, which has been merged.\n\nBoth PRs implement the same \\`db.batch()\\` optimization for D1. #139 is the strict superset:\n- Only one of the four db.batch() candidates to also batch src/routes/admin/categories/+page.server.ts.\n- Uses the correct \\`Promise<{ [K in keyof T]: Awaited<T[K]> }\\>\\` return type on the Database.batch method.\n\nNotable issue with this branch: the commit adds a new file at \\`.jules/bolt.md\\` (lowercase 'j') instead of appending to the existing \\`.Jules/bolt.md\\` (uppercase 'J'). The commit tree contains both blobs, which is a regression — on macOS APFS the lowercase file overwrites the original; on Linux/Cloudflare Pages build (case-sensitive) the two files coexist as unrelated files. #139 (and #133, #134) correctly append to \\`.Jules/bolt.md\\`.\n\nAlso: this branch keeps the unnecessary \\`as [LeanMoveRaw[], ...]\\` cast in src/routes/+page.server.ts:44 because the Database.batch type augmentation was added with a \\`Promise<U>\\` return type that returns the queries, not their results. The correct signature is in #139 (and #133, #134).\n\nThanks for the work — the optimization is real and valuable. Closing to consolidate on the canonical implementation.\" 2>&1 | tail -10","description":"Close PR #132 with reasoning"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-04T00:51:44.125Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/aerialdb && gh pr close 133 --comment \"Closing in favor of #139, which has been merged.\n\nBoth PRs implement the same \\`db.batch()\\` optimization for D1. Of the four parallel candidates, this branch has the cleanest diff (no \\`as any\\` cast, no unused imports), but it does not batch src/routes/admin/categories/+page.server.ts — only #139 covers all three load functions (home, admin dashboard, category management).\n\n#139 also has the correct \\`Promise<{ [K in keyof T]: Awaited<T[K]> }\\>\\` return type and is the most complete implementation.\n\nThanks for the work.\" 2>&1 | tail -3 && echo \"---\" && gh pr close 134 --comment \"Closing in favor of #139, which has been merged.\n\nBoth PRs implement the same \\`db.batch()\\` optimization for D1. This branch has the best test-comment cleanup of the four (it updates the stale \\`featuredMoveRaw\\` reference to \\`featuredMoveResults\\` and removes the obsolete 'Promise.all' comment), but it leaves two unused imports:\n- \\`LeanMoveRaw\\` in src/routes/+page.server.ts:2\n- \\`AdminLeanMoveRaw\\` in src/routes/admin/+page.server.ts:2\n\nThese will fail \\`npm run lint\\` under \\`@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars: 'error'\\`. #139 has those imports removed.\n\nAdditionally, this branch does not batch src/routes/admin/categories/+page.server.ts (only #139 does). #139 also has the correct \\`Promise<{ [K in keyof T]: Awaited<T[K]> }\\>\\` return type on the Database.batch method.\n\nThanks for the work.\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Close PRs #133 and #134"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-04T00:52:04.585Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/aerialdb && gh pr close 135 --comment \"Closing in favor of #138, which has been merged. This was a difficult call because both PRs aim at the same goal (CSP + security headers), and this branch's unique value (admin guard prefix tightening, \\`X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies\\`, expanded \\`Permissions-Policy\\`) is real. However, this branch has a critical production bug:\n\n**CSP at svelte.config.js:21 specifies \\`style-src: [\\\"'self'\\\", 'https://fonts.googleapis.com']\\` WITHOUT \\`'unsafe-inline'\\`.**\n\nPer the SvelteKit docs (\\`/docs/kit/configuration#csp\\`): 'most Svelte transitions work by creating an inline \\`<style>\\` element. If you use these in your app, you must either leave the \\`style-src\\` directive unspecified or add \\`unsafe-inline\\`.'\n\nThe repo currently uses \\`transition:\\` directives in 5 places:\n- src/lib/components/Header.svelte:220 — \\`transition:fade\\`\n- src/lib/components/Header.svelte:285 — \\`transition:slide\\`\n- src/lib/components/Header.svelte:321 — \\`transition:slide\\`\n- src/routes/admin/moves/[id]/edit/+page.svelte:96 — \\`transition:fade\\`\n- src/routes/admin/categories/+page.svelte:227 — \\`transition:fade\\`\n\nMerging this PR as-is would silently break the search slide-down, the move edit fade-in, and the category delete/expand transitions in production.\n\n#138 correctly includes \\`'unsafe-inline'\\` in style-src, adds HSTS preload, the \\`event.setHeaders()\\` logout pattern, and four defensive CSP directives (\\`base-uri\\`, \\`form-action\\`, \\`frame-ancestors: ['none']\\`, \\`upgrade-insecure-requests: true\\`).\n\nIf you want to port this branch's unique value onto #138, the changes are:\n1. Admin guard prefix tightening in src/hooks.server.ts:40-43 (\\`pathname.startsWith('/admin')\\` → \\`pathname === '/admin' || pathname.startsWith('/admin/')\\`) — 3 lines.\n2. Add \\`X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: 'none'\\` to the security headers — 1 line.\n3. Expand \\`Permissions-Policy\\` to include \\`usb=(), interest-cohort=(), screen-wake-lock=()\\` — 1 line.\n4. Update expectedHeaders in src/hooks.server.security.spec.ts to match.\n\nThese can be a small follow-up commit. Thanks for the work — the security intent is solid, the CSP value just needs the inline-style exception.\" 2>&1 | tail -3 && echo \"---\" && gh pr close 131 --comment \"Closing in favor of #136, which has been merged.\n\nBoth PRs modify the same file (src/routes/admin/categories/+page.svelte) to add loading states to the Admin Category Management page. #136 is a strict superset — it includes all of this branch's loading-state changes (Loader2 spinner, \\`isSubmitting\\` / \\`processingId\\` state, button \\`disabled\\` attributes for Create/Update/Delete) plus:\n- \\`aria-invalid\\` attributes on the new-category and edit-category inputs.\n- Input \\`disabled\\` hardening: new-category input disabled during \\`isSubmitting\\`; edit input disabled during \\`processingId === category.id\\`.\n- Row-actions conflict prevention: hides the delete/edit column while the inline edit form is active, preventing conflicting button clicks.\n\nIf this PR had been merged first, #136 would have conflicted on every loading-state region and the resolution would have been 'take #136'. Thanks for the work — the loading-state foundation is in main via #136.\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Close PRs #135 and #131"}}}
