{"timestamp":"2026-06-04T00:54:53.484Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/aerialdb && gh pr close 140 --comment \"Closing — superseded by #139, which has already been merged into dev.\n\nThis branch was created in parallel with the other db.batch() candidates (#132, #133, #134, #139) and branched from the same pre-merge dev head. The db.batch() work is now in dev via #139 (which covers home, admin dashboard, and category management).\n\nThe diff for this branch shows the same work as #139 with a small naming difference (this branch uses \\`featuredMoveRawList\\`, #139 used \\`featuredMoveResults\\`). Merging would either no-op (for identical lines) or conflict on the variable name.\n\nThanks for the work — the optimization is real and already shipping.\" 2>&1 | tail -3 && echo \"---\" && gh pr close 141 --comment \"Closing — mostly superseded by #138, which has already been merged into dev. This branch was created in parallel with the other security-headers candidates (#135, #138) and branched from the same pre-merge dev head.\n\nThe CSP, HSTS preload, and Clear-Site-Data changes are all in dev via #138.\n\nThis branch has one piece of unique value that is NOT in dev: the admin guard path tightening at src/hooks.server.ts — it changes \\`event.url.pathname.startsWith('/admin')\\` to \\`event.url.pathname === '/admin' || event.url.pathname.startsWith('/admin/')\\`, preventing accidental matches on routes like \\`/administration\\`. I noted this as a possible follow-up in the #135 close comment.\n\nIf you'd like this hardening landed, I can do it as a 3-line follow-up commit on dev directly (since the rest of #141 is a duplicate). Just say the word.\n\nNote: this branch's svelte.config.js CSP uses \\`default-src: ['none']\\` vs #138's \\`default-src: ['self']\\`. The former is stricter and may break functionality that isn't explicitly allowed — the safer choice is #138's value, which is what's in dev now.\n\nThanks for the work — the security intent is solid.\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Close #140 and #141 with reasoning"}}}
