{"timestamp":"2026-06-04T00:58:03.287Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"mdocs","args":{"command":"initiative.update","args":{"id":"pr-triage-2026-06-03","progressNote":"## Plan executed — 2026-06-04\n\n### Merged (4 PRs, in order)\n1. #138 — 🛡️ Sentinel: harden security headers and implement CSP\n2. #139 — ⚡ Bolt: optimize database queries with db.batch() (with 3-line pre-merge cleanup: removed unused `LeanMoveRaw` and `AdminLeanMoveRaw` imports, refreshed stale test comment)\n3. #137 — 🎨 Palette: Improve search input consistency and accessibility\n4. #136 — 🎨 Palette: Improve Category Management UX and Accessibility\n\n### Closed without merging (5 PRs from the original 9)\n- #132 — superseded by #139 (had path-case regression `.jules/` vs `.Jules/`, wrong batch return type)\n- #133 — superseded by #139 (missing categories page batching)\n- #134 — superseded by #139 (unused imports would fail lint)\n- #135 — superseded by #138 (CSP `style-src` without `'unsafe-inline'` would have broken 5 Svelte transitions in production)\n- #131 — superseded by #136 (strict subset)\n\n### New PRs that appeared during execution (closed)\nThe agent-spawn duplication pattern is alive in real-time — during the triage (between inventory and merges), two more PRs appeared from parallel Jules tasks:\n- #140 — ⚡ Bolt: Use db.batch() for parallel queries (created 00:29:35, branched from pre-merge dev). Pure duplicate of #139; closed.\n- #141 — 🛡️ Sentinel: security headers and logout hardening (created 00:34:44, branched from pre-merge dev). Mostly duplicate of #138; closed. One unique value (admin guard path tightening) flagged as optional follow-up.\n\n### Validation baseline (post-merge dev)\n- `npm run lint` — passes. 16 warnings, all in mdocs/ and .Jules/ (not code). No warnings in any of the 14 source files my PRs touched.\n- `npm run test:unit --project=server` — 16 files, 85 tests passing.\n- `npm run test:unit --project=client` — 6 files, 30 tests passing.\n- **Total: 115 tests passing** (matches the count #138 cited in its description).\n- `npm run check` — 7 errors remain in test specs (`RequestEvent` type incompatibility in `moves.security.spec.ts` and `categories.security.spec.ts`).\n\n### Pre-existing issue discovered (NOT a regression from the merges)\nThe 7 `npm run check` errors are **pre-existing** — they exist at 6e5a3ea (the pre-merge dev head). Verified by checking out 6e5a3ea and running `npm run check` directly. My merges actually **reduced** the check error count by 1: the logout endpoint's 3-arg `redirect(302, '/', { headers: ... })` form (which was always type-incorrect per the SvelteKit signature) is now fixed by #138's `event.setHeaders({...}); return redirect(302, '/');` refactor.\n\nThis means the AGENTS.md \"Known Validation Baseline\" section is stale: it claims `npm run check` passes cleanly as of 2026-05-30, but the baseline was already broken at 6e5a3ea. The 7 spec errors should be addressed in a separate initiative.\n\n### Final state\n- 4 PRs merged, 7 PRs closed (5 from the original plan + 2 that appeared mid-execution)\n- 0 open duplicate PRs remaining\n- All tests pass; lint is clean for code; 7 pre-existing `npm run check` errors documented\n- One piece of unique value flagged as optional follow-up: admin guard path tightening from #141 (3-line change in src/hooks.server.ts)\n\n### Wiki entry\n`process/agent-pr-spawn-pattern.md` — operational playbook for the recurring duplication pattern. The June 2026 incident (this triage) is added as evidence."}}}}
