{"timestamp":"2026-06-06T01:23:17.328Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"mdocs","args":{"command":"initiative.create","args":{"title":"Admin Guard Path Tightening + Unique #135 Headers","id":"admin-guard-tightening","owner":"system","tags":{"item":["security","admin-guard","hardening","follow-up"]},"objective":"Port the unique value from closed PRs #135 and #141 to dev: (1) tighten the admin guard path check to prevent `/administration` accidental matches, (2) add `X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none`, (3) expand `Permissions-Policy` with `usb=(), interest-cohort=(), screen-wake-lock=()`. Plus update the corresponding test expectations.","plan":"1. Create worktree at /tmp/opencode-worktrees/admin-guard on branch admin-guard-tightening off origin/dev.\n2. Read current src/hooks.server.ts to confirm post-#138 state.\n3. Change `event.url.pathname.startsWith('/admin')` to `pathname === '/admin' || pathname.startsWith('/admin/')` (extract `const path = event.url.pathname;` first).\n4. Add `response.headers.set('X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies', 'none');` to handleSecurityHeaders.\n5. Expand Permissions-Policy string to include `usb=(), interest-cohort=(), screen-wake-lock=()`.\n6. Update src/hooks.server.security.spec.ts expectedHeaders to match.\n7. Verify with `npm run lint` and `npm run test:unit -- --run` — both should remain clean/passing.\n8. Commit to admin-guard-tightening branch. Do NOT push.\n9. Report branch name, file changes, and verification results."}}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-06T01:23:24.380Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"mdocs","args":{"command":"initiative.create","args":{"title":"Fix 7 Pre-existing check Spec Type Errors","id":"fix-pre-existing-check-errors","owner":"system","tags":{"item":["testing","typescript","regression-baseline","follow-up"]},"objective":"Resolve the 7 pre-existing `npm run check` errors in test spec files. The errors are in `src/routes/admin/categories/categories.security.spec.ts:28` (1 error: Cannot find name 'RequestEvent') and `src/routes/admin/moves/moves.security.spec.ts:68,80,94,118,143,165` (6 errors: mock event objects missing RequestEvent properties).","plan":"1. Create worktree at /tmp/opencode-worktrees/fix-check-errors on branch fix-pre-existing-check-errors off origin/dev.\n2. Read the two failing spec files to understand the mock event construction pattern.\n3. Inspect the imports — the test likely needs to import `RequestEvent` from `./$types` or `@sveltejs/kit`.\n4. For each `createMockEvent(...)` call site that doesn't already cast, add `as unknown as RequestEvent` or a typed wrapper. Prefer the minimally invasive fix that preserves test behavior.\n5. If a typed wrapper is cleaner, define a `createTypedMockEvent` helper in the test file.\n6. Verify with `npm run check` — should report 0 errors.\n7. Verify with `npm run test:unit -- --run` — all 115 tests should still pass.\n8. Verify with `npm run lint` — should remain clean.\n9. Commit to fix-pre-existing-check-errors branch. Do NOT push.\n10. Report branch name, files changed, and the new `npm run check` output."}}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-06T01:23:31.363Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"mdocs","args":{"command":"initiative.create","args":{"title":"Update AGENTS.md Validation Baseline","id":"update-agents-md-baseline","owner":"system","tags":{"item":["docs","agents-md","baseline","follow-up"]},"objective":"Update the \"Known Validation Baseline\" section in AGENTS.md to reflect the actual current state of `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run test:unit -- --run` as of 2026-06-04. The 2026-05-30 claim that all three pass cleanly is stale.","plan":"1. Create worktree at /tmp/opencode-worktrees/agents-md-update on branch update-agents-md-baseline off origin/dev.\n2. Read current AGENTS.md to find the \"Known Validation Baseline\" section.\n3. Update it to reflect:\n   - `npm run check` — FAILS with 7 pre-existing spec type errors (mock events missing RequestEvent properties) in `src/routes/admin/categories/categories.security.spec.ts` and `src/routes/admin/moves/moves.security.spec.ts`. A follow-up initiative `fix-pre-existing-check-errors` is open to resolve.\n   - `npm run lint` — passes. 16 warnings, all in `mdocs/` and `.Jules/` files (not in code).\n   - `npm run test:unit -- --run` — passes. 115 tests (85 server, 30 client) all green.\n4. Update the \"As of\" date from 2026-05-30 to 2026-06-04.\n5. Read the updated section back and confirm it accurately describes reality.\n6. Commit to update-agents-md-baseline branch. Do NOT push.\n7. Report branch name and the diff summary."}}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-06T01:23:39.126Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"mdocs","args":{"command":"initiative.create","args":{"title":"Agent-Spawn Pattern Mitigation Research and Plan","id":"agent-spawn-pattern-mitigation","owner":"system","tags":{"item":["process","agent-spawn","guardian","follow-up"]},"objective":"Read the wiki entry `mdocs/wiki/process/agent-pr-spawn-pattern.md` and propose a concrete, prioritized implementation plan for the 4 mitigations it recommends. Focus especially on the Guardian semantic-duplication check (mitigation #2), which is the most impactful.","plan":"1. Read `mdocs/wiki/process/agent-pr-spawn-pattern.md` to understand the 4 mitigations.\n2. Investigate the Guardian agent's source (look in `.opencode/agent/`, `.claude/`, `.Jules/`, or wherever the PR verification agent lives). Determine:\n   - Where Guardian's verification logic is defined.\n   - What checks it currently runs (CI, lint, test).\n   - What hook points exist for adding new checks.\n   - How to add a semantic-duplication check that compares a new PR's file set and commit subject against all open PRs.\n3. For each of the 4 mitigations (single-task-per-topic, semantic-duplication check, branch naming with retry suffix, defensive CSP template), produce a 1-page section with:\n   - Where the change would go (specific file paths).\n   - What the change would look like (code sketch or config change).\n   - Tradeoffs and risks.\n   - Estimated effort (small / medium / large).\n4. Rank the 4 mitigations by ROI and recommend which one(s) to implement first.\n5. Do NOT make any code changes. This is research and proposal only.\n6. Return the full plan as a markdown document."}}}}
