{"timestamp":"2026-06-06T19:57:52.947Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"description":"Update AGENTS.md validation baseline","prompt":"You are a subagent updating the AGENTS.md documentation for the AerialDB repo at `/Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/aerialdb`.\n\n## Objective\n\nThe \"Known Validation Baseline\" section in `AGENTS.md` is stale. As of 2026-05-30 it claims these commands pass cleanly:\n- `npm run check`\n- `npm run lint`\n- `npm run test:unit -- --run`\n\nVerified on 2026-06-04 against the current `dev` branch (post-PR-triage merge):\n\n| Command | Actual state |\n|---|---|\n| `npm run check` | **FAILS** with 7 pre-existing TypeScript errors in test spec files. Errors are at `src/routes/admin/categories/categories.security.spec.ts:28:19` (Cannot find name 'RequestEvent') and `src/routes/admin/moves/moves.security.spec.ts:68,80,94,118,143,165` (6 errors: mock event objects missing RequestEvent properties). These are pre-existing as of commit 6e5a3ea — not caused by the recent PR merges. A follow-up initiative `fix-pre-existing-check-errors` is in flight. |\n| `npm run lint` | **PASSES.** 16 warnings, all in `mdocs/` and `.Jules/` files. Zero warnings in code files. |\n| `npm run test:unit -- --run` | **PASSES.** 115 tests (85 server + 30 client) all green. |\n\n## Setup\n\n- Work in a worktree: `git worktree add /tmp/opencode-worktrees/agents-md-update -b update-agents-md-baseline origin/dev`\n- Inside the worktree: `cd /tmp/opencode-worktrees/agents-md-update`\n- Read the current `AGENTS.md` to find the \"Known Validation Baseline\" section (search for \"Validation\" or \"Baseline\").\n\n## What to update\n\nReplace the \"Known Validation Baseline\" section with one that reflects reality. Suggested structure (you can refine the wording, but keep the facts):\n\n```\n## Known Validation Baseline\n\nAs of 2026-06-04 (post the 4-PR merge of #138/#139/#137/#136), the\nbaseline state of these commands is:\n\n- `npm run check` — **fails** with 7 pre-existing TypeScript errors\n  in test spec files. The errors are mock event objects missing\n  `RequestEvent` properties in\n  `src/routes/admin/categories/categories.security.spec.ts:28` and\n  `src/routes/admin/moves/moves.security.spec.ts:68,80,94,118,143,165`.\n  These are pre-existing as of commit 6e5a3ea (the most recent dev\n  commit before the 4-PR merge) and are unrelated to application code.\n  Follow-up initiative `fix-pre-existing-check-errors` is in flight.\n\n- `npm run lint` — **passes.** 16 warnings remain, all in\n  `mdocs/` and `.Jules/` files (managed by the mdocs plugin and the\n  Jules agent notes), zero in code.\n\n- `npm run test:unit -- --run` — **passes.** 115 tests\n  (85 server + 30 client) all green.\n\nWhen adding a new PR, treat a check failure as a regression only if\nthe failing line is touched by the PR. The 7 pre-existing spec errors\nare not regressions; they predate the baseline.\n```\n\nAdjust wording to match the rest of AGENTS.md's voice and conventions. Keep the markdown formatting (tabs for indent per the project style — check by reading the file).\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter updating:\n- Read back the updated section to confirm it accurately describes reality.\n- Run from the worktree:\n  - `npm run check` — should still report 7 errors (we're only updating docs, not code).\n  - `npm run lint` — should still be clean for code (the 16 mdocs warnings are pre-existing).\n  - `npm run test:unit -- --run` — should still be 115/115.\n\nThese are sanity checks; they should match the documented state.\n\n## Commit\n\nAfter verification passes, commit your changes with a clear message:\n```\ndocs: update AGENTS.md validation baseline to 2026-06-04\n\nThe 2026-05-30 claim that `npm run check` passes cleanly is stale.\nAs of 2026-06-04 (post the 4-PR merge of #138/#139/#137/#136), the\nbaseline is:\n- `npm run check` — fails with 7 pre-existing spec type errors\n  (mock event RequestEvent type incompatibility); not from the\n  recent merges. Follow-up `fix-pre-existing-check-errors` open.\n- `npm run lint` — passes (16 mdocs/.Jules warnings, 0 in code).\n- `npm run test:unit -- --run` — passes (115 tests).\n```\n\n**Do NOT push to origin.** I will review and push/merge.\n\n## Return format\n\nYour final message must contain:\n1. **Branch name:** `update-agents-md-baseline`\n2. **Worktree path:** `/tmp/opencode-worktrees/agents-md-update`\n3. **Commit SHA:** (output of `git rev-parse HEAD` in the worktree)\n4. **Diff summary:** the actual `--- a/AGENTS.md` and `+++ b/AGENTS.md` section that changed, with the old and new text\n5. **Verification results:** literal output of `npm run check` and `npm run test:unit -- --run` (should be unchanged)\n6. **Any anomalies or notes.**","subagent_type":"DocWriter"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-06T20:18:02.161Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"description":"Fix 7 pre-existing check spec errors","prompt":"You are a subagent fixing 7 pre-existing TypeScript type errors in the AerialDB test suite at `/Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/aerialdb`.\n\n## Objective\n\nResolve these 7 errors that `npm run check` reports on the post-merge `dev` branch:\n\n1. `src/routes/admin/categories/categories.security.spec.ts:28:19` — **Error: Cannot find name 'RequestEvent'.** The test uses a type annotation `as unknown as RequestEvent` but does not import the `RequestEvent` type.\n\n2. `src/routes/admin/moves/moves.security.spec.ts:68:30, 80:49, 94:30, 118:30, 143:30, 165:30` — **6 errors** of the form: `Argument of type '{ request: { formData: Mock<Procedure>; }; locals: { user: any; }; params: any; fetch: Mock<Procedure>; platform: {}; }' is not assignable to parameter of type 'RequestEvent<RouteParams, ...>'.` The mock event object is missing required properties (`cookies`, `getClientAddress`, `route`, `setHeaders`, and 5 more) from the full `RequestEvent` type.\n\nThese errors are pre-existing as of commit 6e5a3ea (pre-merge dev) and are not caused by the recent PR merges. Your job is to fix them in a separate branch so the next triage session has a clean baseline.\n\n## Setup\n\n- Work in a worktree: `git worktree add /tmp/opencode-worktrees/fix-check-errors -b fix-pre-existing-check-errors origin/dev`\n- Inside the worktree: `cd /tmp/opencode-worktrees/fix-check-errors`\n- Read both failing spec files to understand the mock event construction pattern.\n\n## Approach\n\nLook at how `createMockEvent` is defined in each test file. The mock is hand-rolled (not using SvelteKit's testing utilities). Two acceptable approaches:\n\n**Option A (minimal):** Add `as unknown as RequestEvent` (or `as unknown as RequestEvent<RouteParams, '/admin/moves/new'>` for route-specific events) at each call site. The test files likely already have one or two such casts; just ensure all of them are present and the type is imported.\n\n**Option B (cleaner):** Define a typed `createTypedMockEvent` helper at the top of each test file that returns a fully-typed `RequestEvent`. Replace all `createMockEvent` calls in that file with the typed version. This is more invasive but more type-safe.\n\nPrefer **Option A** if it's the smallest change. Use **Option B** if the type annotations are too verbose at every call site (i.e., each call site needs a different `RouteParams`).\n\nFor the `categories.security.spec.ts:28` import error, add the import:\n```ts\nimport type { RequestEvent } from './$types';\n```\n(or import from `@sveltejs/kit` if the `$types` re-export is not available — check what works).\n\n## Important: do NOT change test behavior\n\nThe tests should still pass. Don't change the mock's runtime values, just fix the type annotation. After your changes, `npm run test:unit -- --run` should still report 115 passing tests.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun from the worktree:\n- `npm run check` — should report **0 errors** (down from 7).\n- `npm run test:unit -- --run` — should report **115 tests passing** (unchanged).\n- `npm run lint` — should remain clean for code files.\n\n## Commit\n\nAfter verification passes, commit your changes with a clear message:\n```\ntest: fix RequestEvent type annotations in security specs\n\n- Add `import type { RequestEvent }` to categories.security.spec.ts\n  (line 28 had `as unknown as RequestEvent` without the import).\n- Add `as unknown as RequestEvent<...>` casts to 6 mock event calls\n  in moves.security.spec.ts (lines 68, 80, 94, 118, 143, 165) to\n  satisfy the full RequestEvent type signature.\n- No test behavior change — all 115 tests still pass.\n- `npm run check` now reports 0 errors.\n```\n\n**Do NOT push to origin.** I will review and push/merge.\n\n## Return format\n\nYour final message must contain:\n1. **Branch name:** `fix-pre-existing-check-errors`\n2. **Worktree path:** `/tmp/opencode-worktrees/fix-check-errors`\n3. **Commit SHA:** (output of `git rev-parse HEAD` in the worktree)\n4. **Files changed:** list with line counts (output of `git diff --stat origin/dev`)\n5. **Approach used:** Option A or Option B, and why\n6. **Verification results:** literal output (last 5-10 lines) of `npm run check`, `npm run test:unit -- --run`, and `npm run lint`\n7. **Any anomalies or notes** — e.g., if a test file uses a different mock pattern than expected.","subagent_type":"TestEngineer"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-06-06T20:18:02.211Z","type":"tool","step":"IDLE","details":{"toolName":"task","args":{"description":"Fix TypeScript type errors","prompt":"You are executing a focused fix on the AerialDB repository at `/Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/aerialdb`. The repo is on `main` (or possibly `master`) and `origin/dev` is a branch that has 7 pre-existing TypeScript type errors in 2 test files. Your job: create a worktree, fix the errors, run verification, commit (but do NOT push), and return precise results.\n\n## Step 1 — Create the worktree\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/bbaaxx/Code/projects/aerialdb\ngit fetch origin dev 2>&1 | tail -5 || true\ngit worktree add /tmp/opencode-worktrees/fix-check-errors -b fix-pre-existing-check-errors origin/dev 2>&1\ncd /tmp/opencode-worktrees/fix-check-errors\ngit status\ngit log -1 --oneline\n```\n\nIf the directory `/tmp/opencode-worktrees/fix-check-errors` already exists, remove it first with `git worktree remove --force /tmp/opencode-worktrees/fix-check-errors` and `rm -rf /tmp/opencode-worktrees/fix-check-errors`.\n\nVerify you are now in the new worktree. All subsequent commands should run from `/tmp/opencode-worktrees/fix-check-errors`.\n\n## Step 2 — Confirm the 7 errors exist on the baseline\n\nRun from the worktree:\n```bash\nnpm run check 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\n\nYou should see 7 type errors. If you see 0 errors, STOP and report that — the baseline is already clean. If you see different errors, STOP and report them verbatim.\n\n## Step 3 — Read the failing files (to confirm your understanding)\n\nRead these files:\n- `src/routes/admin/categories/categories.security.spec.ts` (103 lines, error at line 28)\n- `src/routes/admin/moves/moves.security.spec.ts` (173 lines, errors at lines 68, 80, 94, 118, 143, 165)\n\nThe first file uses `as unknown as RequestEvent` on line 28 but does NOT import `RequestEvent` anywhere. The second file's `createMockEvent` function returns a partial object that's missing many required properties of `RequestEvent` (cookies, getClientAddress, route, setHeaders, etc.).\n\n## Step 4 — Apply the fixes (Option A: minimal)\n\n### Fix 1: `src/routes/admin/categories/categories.security.spec.ts`\n\nAdd a single import line. After the existing import block (line 3, which is `import { isRedirect } from '@sveltejs/kit';`), add:\n```ts\nimport type { RequestEvent } from '@sveltejs/kit';\n```\n\n(Use the `@sveltejs/kit` import, NOT `./$types`, because this is a generic `RequestEvent` not tied to a specific route. The cast on line 28 uses bare `RequestEvent` with no generic args.)\n\nSo lines 1-4 become:\n```ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from 'vitest';\nimport { actions } from './+page.server';\nimport { isRedirect } from '@sveltejs/kit';\nimport type { RequestEvent } from '@sveltejs/kit';\n```\n\nDo NOT change any other line in this file.\n\n### Fix 2: `src/routes/admin/moves/moves.security.spec.ts`\n\n**Add the import** at the top of the file. After line 25 (`import { isRedirect } from '@sveltejs/kit';`), add:\n```ts\nimport type { RequestEvent } from '@sveltejs/kit';\n```\n\n**Modify `createMockEvent`** (currently lines 42-55) to add an `as unknown as RequestEvent` cast to its return value. The new function body should end with `}; } as unknown as RequestEvent;` instead of just `}; }`. Specifically, change the closing `}` and `}` so the final return is:\n\n```ts\nfunction createMockEvent(formData: FormData, user: any = null, params: any = {}) {\n    return {\n        request: {\n            formData: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(formData)\n        },\n        locals: { user },\n        params,\n        fetch: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({\n            ok: true,\n            json: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ url: 'http://example.com/image.jpg' })\n        }),\n        platform: {}\n    } as unknown as RequestEvent;\n}\n```\n\n**Do NOT remove** the existing `as unknown as Parameters<typeof ...>[0]` casts on lines ~59-61, ~109-111, and ~156-158. They become redundant but are harmless and removing them is out of scope. Leaving them keeps the diff minimal and preserves the original intent.\n\nDo NOT change the runtime values of any test (no `expect`, no `vi.fn`, no FormData, no assertion logic — all stay the same).\n\n## Step 5 — Verify the fixes\n\nFrom the worktree, run:\n```bash\nnpm run check 2>&1 | tail -20\n```\n\nYou should see `0 errors`. If there are still errors, STOP and report them verbatim. Do not commit yet.\n\n```bash\nnpm run test:unit -- --run 2>&1 | tail -30\n```\n\nYou should see `115 passed` tests (or similar — the prompt says 115). Capture the final summary line.\n\n```bash\nnpm run lint 2>&1 | tail -20\n```\n\nShould remain clean for the two changed files (or all files). Report any warnings/errors.\n\n## Step 6 — Commit (do NOT push)\n\n```bash\ngit diff --stat origin/dev\ngit add -A\ngit commit -m \"test: fix RequestEvent type annotations in security specs\n\n- Add \\`import type { RequestEvent }\\` to categories.security.spec.ts\n  (line 28 had \\`as unknown as RequestEvent\\` without the import).\n- Add \\`as unknown as RequestEvent\\` cast to createMockEvent's return\n  in moves.security.spec.ts to satisfy the full RequestEvent type\n  signature. This resolves 6 errors at lines 68, 80, 94, 118, 143, 165.\n- No test behavior change — all 115 tests still pass.\n- \\`npm run check\\` now reports 0 errors.\"\ngit rev-parse HEAD\ngit log -1 --oneline\ngit status\n```\n\nDo NOT run `git push`. The user will review and push.\n\n## Step 7 — Return this exact information in your final message\n\n1. **Branch name:** `fix-pre-existing-check-errors`\n2. **Worktree path:** `/tmp/opencode-worktrees/fix-check-errors`\n3. **Commit SHA:** (output of `git rev-parse HEAD`)\n4. **Files changed:** (output of `git diff --stat origin/dev`)\n5. **Verification results — copy verbatim the last 10 lines of:**\n   - `npm run check`\n   - `npm run test:unit -- --run`\n   - `npm run lint`\n6. **Notes:** Anything unexpected (e.